<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36431" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piscŭlentus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of fishes</i>, <i>abounding in fish</i>
			(ante- and postclass.): fluvius, Cato ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 151, 7 sq.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">loca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Rud. 4, 2, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">promuntorium omnibus mari nantibus
					pisculentissimum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 5, 6</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piscŭlentum</span></b> , i, n.,
				<i>a remedy prepared from fish</i>,
					<i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 294, 40</span></i>.</div>
